This is the entire change TrekSafe makes to upstream Meshtastic. Two lines, in
one file. Everything else lives in this repo and is symlinked into the upstream
tree at build time, which is what D1 means by a module rather than a fork: when
Meshtastic ships a release you pull it, reapply two lines, and carry on.

The context below is from src/modules/Modules.cpp on the master branch as of
August 2026. Upstream moves this file often. If the patch does not apply, do
not fight it, make the two changes by hand:

  1. add     #include "modules/TrekSafe/TrekSafeModule.h"    with the other
             module includes at the top
  2. add     trekSafeModule = new TrekSafeModule();          inside
             setupModules(), in the section that runs when the device is not
             in router-only mode

Keeping this to two lines is the point. If it ever grows past a handful, that
is the signal that D1 deserves re-opening, not a reason to quietly fork.

--- a/src/modules/Modules.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/Modules.cpp
@@
 #include "modules/NodeInfoModule.h"
 #include "modules/PositionModule.h"
+#include "modules/TrekSafe/TrekSafeModule.h"
 #include "modules/RoutingModule.h"
 #include "modules/TextMessageModule.h"
@@
     nodeInfoModule = new NodeInfoModule();
     positionModule = new PositionModule();
+    trekSafeModule = new TrekSafeModule(TrekSafeModule::ROLE_BEACON);
     waypointModule = new WaypointModule();
